prompt_sent: Your Task:
Your task is to transcribe the text from all the images in sequence. Give me the full transcription formatted properly for markdown, make sure everything is included. No commentary.

The goal is to produce a clean, readable, and structurally rich document using precise Markdown formatting. You will act as both a transcriber and a document formatter.
Primary Directive: Content and Flow
Reconstruct Paragraphs: This is the most important rule. Ignore the original line breaks from the image. Combine lines of text to form complete, flowing paragraphs.
Join Hyphenated Words: If a word is split with a hyphen at the end of a line, reconstruct it into a single word.
Identify True Paragraph Breaks: Apply paragraph breaks only where they exist in the original text, typically indicated by indentation or significant vertical spacing between text blocks.
Detailed Markdown Formatting Instructions:
You must scan the source text for the following structural and stylistic elements and apply the corresponding Markdown syntax.
Headings:
Identify the main title of the document and format it as a Heading 1 (#).
Identify major section titles and format them as a Heading 2 (##).
Identify subsection titles and format them as a Heading 3 (###). Use your judgment for deeper-level headings (####).


Emphasis:
For text that is italicized in the source, use single asterisks: *text*.
For text that is bold in the source, use double asterisks: **text**.
For text that is both bold and italicized, use triple asterisks: ***text***.


Lists:
Unordered Lists: If you find a bulleted list (using symbols like •, -, or *), transcribe it as a Markdown unordered list using hyphens (-).
Ordered Lists: If you find a numbered list (e.g., 1., 2., a., b.), transcribe it as a Markdown ordered list (1., 2., 3.).
Nested Lists: Pay close attention to indentation to correctly represent nested list items.


Blockquotes:
If a section of text is indented or visually set apart as a quotation, format it as a blockquote by prefixing each line with > .


Horizontal Rules:
If the original document uses a distinct line or a series of characters (like *** or ---) to visually separate sections of text, represent this with a Markdown horizontal rule (---).


Strikethrough:
For any text that has a line through it, use tildes to format it as strikethrough: ~~text~~.


Content Cleanup Rules:
Exclude Extraneous Elements: Strictly omit page numbers, headers, footers, and any handwritten or printed marginalia.
Correct Obvious Errors: Silently fix any clear spelling or grammatical errors found in the source text.
Final Output Requirements:
The output must be only the transcribed text formatted in pure Markdown.
Do not include any introductory phrases, explanations, or commentary in your response. Begin directly with the transcribed content.
If there is no text present in the image to transcribe, output a blank text, don’t write anything, leave it empty.
